# BIOS firmware layer: intentions for machines that boot via BIOS.
#
# Intentions ONLY. The package manager owns dependency closure; never
# enumerate resolved dependencies here (saphira-profiles(5)).
#
# BIOS needs nothing beyond the common set: GRUB covers the i386-pc
# target from the same package that covers x86_64-efi, there is no
# NVRAM to manage and no FAT system partition to maintain, so there
# is deliberately no package list here. This file exists so the
# firmware dimension is explicit and reviewable: saphira-image appends
# base-bios to bios-* targets and base-efi to uefi-* targets, and a
# future BIOS-specific need has a home that is not a generic profile.
# An empty layer resolves to nothing, which for BIOS is the correct
# closure, not an oversight.
